# wisp

a way to move files over the internet using only a **dht** and **tcp**

no stun, turn, webrtc, signaling server or 3rd party services

the dht is for finding peers
after that its tcp doing tcp things

## why

because i wanted to see if it could be done

## more on wisp

this is **not** trying to replace croc
or literally anything else similar

if youre looking for something that isnt broken go use one of those

## what about nat

wisp doesnt do stun because *wisp isnt stun protocol*

if two peers cant make a tcp connection then youre probably not transferring anything today

given my implementation works on around 90% of all global networks and may bypass certain firewalls but the remaining 10% is private networks or symmetric nat

